[200.401095, "o", "# MLService Deployment Fix\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\nService failed with \"No module named 'tokenizers'\" even though:\r\n- tokenizers was in requirements.txt\r\n- pip install -r requirements.txt exited successfully\r\n- `python -c \"import tokenizers\"` worked fine\r\n\r\n## Root Causes\r\n\r\n1. **Shell alias override**: `~/.bashrc` contained `alias python='/usr/bin/python3'` which forced all `python` commands to use the system Python instead of the virtual environment Python, even when the venv was activated.\r\n\r\n2. **Wrong working directory**: The service must be run from `/home/user` (parent directory), not from `/home/user/mlservice`, because Python's `-m` flag needs to find the `mlservice` package in the Python path.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\n### Fixed Issues:\r\n1. Commented out the problematic alias in `~/.bashrc`:\r\n   ```bash\r\n   #alias python='/usr/bin/python3'\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n2. Created `start.sh` launcher script that:\r\n   - Changes to the correct working directory (`/home/user`)\r\n   - Activates the virtual environment\r\n   - Runs the service"]
[200.40118, "o", " with the venv's Python\r\n\r\n### Production Deployment\r\n\r\n**Use the launcher script:**\r\n```bash\r\n/home/user/mlservice/start.sh\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Or manually:**\r\n```bash\r\ncd /home/user\r\nsource mlservice/.venv/bin/activate\r\npython -m mlservice\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Important:** Always run from `/home/user`, NOT from `/home/user/mlservice`!\r\n\r\n## Why It Seemed to Work Sometimes\r\n\r\nThe `python -c \"import tokenizers\"` test passed because:\r\n- It was using the system Python (due to the alias)\r\n- The system Python happened to have tokenizers installed globally\r\n- But the service needed the venv's packages, which weren't accessible through the aliased Python\r\n\r\n"]
[200.401318, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
